2025-05-20 09:16:31,273 - INFO -       "implication_title": "Bifurcation of Trust and Regulation: Emergence of Transnational Consulting ‘Commons’ and Parallel Shadow Markets",
2025-05-20 09:16:31,291 - INFO -       "implication_description": "Cross-industry integration (SOI-001/SOI-004), rise of global risk ecosystems (SOI-003), and intensified client power/platformization (SOI-006) interact with fragmented geopolitical/regulatory environments to create a bifurcated consulting landscape. On one side, highly regulated, credentialed, transparent 'consulting commons' operate under open protocols and industry-wide ESG/AI/ethics standards—trusted by major enterprises and regulators alike. On the other, a parallel shadow market for opaque, high-risk, or regionally non-compliant advisory services flourishes, fueled by AI-driven anonymization, modular service delivery, and 'grey zone' talents. The rules of the game fundamentally change: navigating credentialed and shadow advisory ecosystems becomes a risk/reward management exercise for clients, not just a procurement choice. Regulatory authority and trust become portable, negotiated commodities.",
