2025-05-20 09:16:32,572 - INFO -       "implication_title": "Societal Revaluation of Expertise: Consulting as Civic Utility or Public Good",
2025-05-20 09:16:32,590 - INFO -       "implication_description": "The widespread adoption of ESG-centric, tech-driven smart city solutions (SOI-004), the elevation of consulting as an embedded infrastructure (SOI-002), and the transformation of talent models (SOI-005) interact with shifting societal expectations around transparency, sustainability, and inclusion. The result is a profound redefinition of consulting’s societal role—from commercial service to strategic civic utility. Governments and international bodies increasingly treat consulting as critical infrastructure, subject to public standard-setting, universal access, transparency requirements, and civic oversight (analogous to utilities or public audit authorities). This shifts consulting from pure private sector optimization to enabler of systemic public or quasi-public value—reshaping business, talent, and value realization models.",
